{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_014Jz2b3yXsc33uTBAAvxYZQ","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# 2026-04-15-2230-prealloc-whir-fold-buffers\n2\t\n3\tPre-allocate and reuse WHIR sumcheck fold buffers (`f_coeffs`, `w_moments`) via a pingpong pattern instead of allocating new DeviceBuffers each inner round. Currently, each of the k_whir × num_whir_rounds inner sumcheck rounds allocates two fresh DeviceBuffers (one for folded `f_coeffs`, one for folded `w_moments`) and frees the previous pair. For the first ~5 rounds at APC 300 (buffer sizes 128-16 MiB), these go through VPMM, creating page churn that disturbs GPU memory pool state for subsequent bandwidth-bound phases. The WHIR phase regressed 25ms from baseline (100ms → 125ms) coinciding with VPMM page size changes, suggesting pool state sensitivity. Pre-allocating at maximum size and alternating between two buffer pairs eliminates all per-round VPMM allocations/frees and stabilizes pool state.\n4\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8773bab9-c899-4b31-8324-e4269b1a66cf","uuid":"1d2c4ad4-da89-4aae-bb6d-fbbdeef04e29","timestamp":"2026-04-15T22:20:38.632Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt-results/task.md","content":"# 2026-04-15-2230-prealloc-whir-fold-buffers\n\nPre-allocate and reuse WHIR sumcheck fold buffers (`f_coeffs`, `w_moments`) via a pingpong pattern instead of allocating new DeviceBuffers each inner round. Currently, each of the k_whir × num_whir_rounds inner sumcheck rounds allocates two fresh DeviceBuffers (one for folded `f_coeffs`, one for folded `w_moments`) and frees the previous pair. For the first ~5 rounds at APC 300 (buffer sizes 128-16 MiB), these go through VPMM, creating page churn that disturbs GPU memory pool state for subsequent bandwidth-bound phases. The WHIR phase regressed 25ms from baseline (100ms → 125ms) coinciding with VPMM page size changes, suggesting pool state sensitivity. Pre-allocating at maximum size and alternating between two buffer pairs eliminates all per-round VPMM allocations/frees and stabilizes pool state.\n","numLines":4,"startLine":1,"totalLines":4}}}
