{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01L7doJLjz5syn59p8hebr2y","type":"tool_result","content":"22\tpub struct DeviceBuffer<T> {\n23\t    ptr: *mut T,\n24\t    len: usize,\n25\t    owns_memory: bool,\n26\t}\n27\t\n28\t/// A struct that packs a pointer with a size in bytes to pass on CUDA.\n29\t/// It holds `*const c_void` for being a universal simple type that can be read by CUDA.\n30\t/// Since it is hard to enforce immutability preservation, it just holds `*const`,\n31\t/// but has two separate constructors for more robustness from the usage perspective.\n32\t/// This is essentially a [DeviceBuffer] but without owning the data.\n33\t#[repr(C)]\n34\t#[derive(Debug, Copy, Clone)]\n35\tpub struct DeviceBufferView {\n36\t    pub ptr: *const c_void,\n37\t    pub size: usize,\n38\t}\n39\t\n40\tunsafe impl<T> Send for DeviceBuffer<T> {}\n41\tunsafe impl<T> Sync for DeviceBuffer<T> {}\n42\t\n43\timpl<T> DeviceBuffer<T> {\n44\t    /// Creates an \"empty\" DeviceBuffer with a null pointer and zero length.\n45\t    #[allow(clippy::new_without_default)]\n46\t    pub fn new() -> Self {\n47\t        DeviceBuffer {\n48\t            ptr: ptr::null_mut(),\n49\t            len: 0,\n50\t            owns_memory: true,\n51\t        }\n52\t    }\n53\t\n54\t    /// # Safety\n55\t    /// - The caller must ensure that the pointer `ptr` is valid for `len` elements of type `T` in\n56\t    ///   device memory.\n57\t    /// - Dropping the constructed buffer will attempt to free the memory. As such, `ptr` must\n58\t    ///   either have been allocated by the internal memory manager (VPMM) or the caller must use\n59\t    ///   `ManuallyDrop` to prevent double-free.\n60\t    pub unsafe fn from_raw_parts(ptr: *mut T, len: usize) -> Self {\n61\t        DeviceBuffer {\n62\t            ptr,\n63\t            len,\n64\t            owns_memory: true,\n65\t        }\n66\t    }\n67\t\n68\t    /// Creates a non-owning view into device memory. The view will NOT free the memory on drop.\n69\t    ///\n70\t    /// # Safety\n71\t    /// The caller must ensure that:\n72\t    /// - `ptr` points to valid device memory for `len` elements of type `T`\n73\t    /// - The underlying memory remains valid for the lifetime of this buffer\n74\t    pub unsafe fn non_owning(ptr: *mut T, len: usize) -> Self {\n75\t        DeviceBuffer {\n76\t            ptr,\n77\t            len,\n78\t            owns_memory: false,\n79\t        }\n80\t    }\n81\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8773bab9-c899-4b31-8324-e4269b1a66cf","uuid":"3eecd123-b6c7-4bd0-b6ac-d483c978b683","timestamp":"2026-04-15T22:59:09.205Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/georg/stark-backend/crates/cuda-common/src/d_buffer.rs","content":"pub struct DeviceBuffer<T> {\n    ptr: *mut T,\n    len: usize,\n    owns_memory: bool,\n}\n\n/// A struct that packs a pointer with a size in bytes to pass on CUDA.\n/// It holds `*const c_void` for being a universal simple type that can be read by CUDA.\n/// Since it is hard to enforce immutability preservation, it just holds `*const`,\n/// but has two separate constructors for more robustness from the usage perspective.\n/// This is essentially a [DeviceBuffer] but without owning the data.\n#[repr(C)]\n#[derive(Debug, Copy, Clone)]\npub struct DeviceBufferView {\n    pub ptr: *const c_void,\n    pub size: usize,\n}\n\nunsafe impl<T> Send for DeviceBuffer<T> {}\nunsafe impl<T> Sync for DeviceBuffer<T> {}\n\nimpl<T> DeviceBuffer<T> {\n    /// Creates an \"empty\" DeviceBuffer with a null pointer and zero length.\n    #[allow(clippy::new_without_default)]\n    pub fn new() -> Self {\n        DeviceBuffer {\n            ptr: ptr::null_mut(),\n            len: 0,\n            owns_memory: true,\n        }\n    }\n\n    /// # Safety\n    /// - The caller must ensure that the pointer `ptr` is valid for `len` elements of type `T` in\n    ///   device memory.\n    /// - Dropping the constructed buffer will attempt to free the memory. As such, `ptr` must\n    ///   either have been allocated by the internal memory manager (VPMM) or the caller must use\n    ///   `ManuallyDrop` to prevent double-free.\n    pub unsafe fn from_raw_parts(ptr: *mut T, len: usize) -> Self {\n        DeviceBuffer {\n            ptr,\n            len,\n            owns_memory: true,\n        }\n    }\n\n    /// Creates a non-owning view into device memory. The view will NOT free the memory on drop.\n    ///\n    /// # Safety\n    /// The caller must ensure that:\n    /// - `ptr` points to valid device memory for `len` elements of type `T`\n    /// - The underlying memory remains valid for the lifetime of this buffer\n    pub unsafe fn non_owning(ptr: *mut T, len: usize) -> Self {\n        DeviceBuffer {\n            ptr,\n            len,\n            owns_memory: false,\n        }\n    }\n","numLines":60,"startLine":22,"totalLines":243}}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01UrRfQw15H5UWSy57YjUfy4","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I see: DeviceBuffer has `ptr`, `len`, and `owns_memory`. The `len` field IS the capacity — there's no separate capacity. When you do `with_capacity(n)`, it allocates n elements and sets len = n.\n\nFor reusing buffers: if I have a buffer of len=2^20 and I want to use it for a 2^19 fold output, I need to create a non-owning view of the first 2^19 elements. Then the CUDA kernel writes to the first 2^19 elements.\n\nBut creating non-owning views is unsafe and requires careful lifetime management.\n\n\nI should look at how the existing pingpong MLE fold optimization handles this pattern. Rather than continuing to analyze, I'll write up a concrete proposal: reuse fold buffers across WHIR inner rounds using non-owning DeviceBuffer views, plus pre-allocate g_coeffs across outer rounds. The estimated savings are modest (5-15ms), but this is the most practical optimization I can achieve right now. I'll get it reviewed and let that process either validate the approach or surface other opportunities.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1096,"cache_read_input_tokens":197856,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1096},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8773bab9-c899-4b31-8324-e4269b1a66cf","uuid":"49ac5838-81fb-48cb-a75e-1b25ef3403e9"}
