{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01AotEBQUyK7Nabe6EENK9YM","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# 2026-04-16-0030-reuse-whir-buffers-inplace-fold\n2\t\n3\tReduce WHIR opening proof overhead by reusing f_coeffs and w_moments buffers across outer WHIR rounds (avoiding re-allocation when capacity suffices) and folding in-place within inner rounds (eliminating per-round allocation of new output buffers). Nsight profiling confirms WHIR GPU kernel times are identical between baseline (46ms) and current (46ms), but wall clock regressed from 100ms to 125ms — the 25ms regression is entirely from non-kernel overhead (allocation churn, sync latency). This optimization targets the allocation-related portion of that overhead.\n4\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01HcBKhSQwJHvKPfX49TuAKt","session_id":"8773bab9-c899-4b31-8324-e4269b1a66cf","uuid":"928ba6fc-c5ee-4758-8f9c-4bff6f1d537b","timestamp":"2026-04-15T23:00:52.851Z"}
