ead) eliminates unnecessary synchronization infrastructure in single-threaded phases and removes a contention source in multi-threaded phases.","+Hoist the per-trace `TraceCtx` construction (including `main_ptrs.to_device()` uploads) out of the MLE round loop in `prove_zerocheck_and_logup_gpu`. Currently, each MLE round reconstructs `early_eval` and `late_eval` vectors from scratch, performing ~300 `to_device()` calls per round at APC 300 to upload pointer arrays that don't change between rounds. With 14 rounds × 2 segments = 28 iterations, this creates ~8,400 redundant allocation+upload cycles. Hoisting the `TraceCtx` construction before the MLE loop and reusing the device pointer buffers across rounds eliminates this per-round overhead."]}],"originalFile":"# 2026-04-16-0030-eliminate-copy-event-mutex-stark-path\n\nReplace global COPY_EVENT mutex-based `to_host()` calls with lock-free `to_host_on_current_stream()` throughout the STARK excl trace hot path (Constraints + Openings + Trace Commit). The current `to_host()` acquires a global Mutex, records a CUDA event, and synchronizes via `cudaEventSynchronize` — adding ~12.7μs overhead per call plus mutex contention potential. Nsight shows 3845 `cudaEventSynchronize` calls totaling 49ms and 4864 `cudaEventRecord` calls totaling 7ms across the full proof. Converting STARK excl trace hot-path calls to `to_host_on_current_stream()` (which uses direct `cudaStreamSynchronize` without mutex or event overhead) eliminates unnecessary synchronization infrastructure in single-threaded phases and removes a contention source in multi-threaded phases.\n"}}
