{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01SxixPQBs5NcyJq6nMjdZjM","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# 2026-04-16-0030-hoist-mle-trace-ctx-construction\n2\t\n3\tHoist the per-trace `TraceCtx` construction (including `main_ptrs.to_device()` uploads) out of the MLE round loop in `prove_zerocheck_and_logup_gpu`. Currently, each MLE round reconstructs `early_eval` and `late_eval` vectors from scratch, performing ~300 `to_device()` calls per round at APC 300 to upload pointer arrays that don't change between rounds. With 14 rounds × 2 segments = 28 iterations, this creates ~8,400 redundant allocation+upload cycles. Hoisting the `TraceCtx` construction before the MLE loop and reusing the device pointer buffers across rounds eliminates this per-round overhead.\n4\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01FEaHnKTkJi1aZs7VhUfxJN","session_id":"8773bab9-c899-4b31-8324-e4269b1a66cf","uuid":"fd11c5ad-5c69-4a9b-8538-0df54322d883","timestamp":"2026-04-15T23:13:17.049Z"}
