{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01WZhDwVGzs3xixwvwoX7RSr","type":"tool_result","content":"650\t    // - each round the prover needs to compute univariate polynomial `s_round`. This poly is linear\n651\t    //   since we are taking MLE of `evals`.\n652\t    // - at end of each round, sample random `r_round` in `EF`\n653\t    //\n654\t    // `s_round` is degree `s_deg` so we evaluate it at `0, ..., =s_deg`. The prover skips\n655\t    // evaluation at `0` because the verifier can infer it from the previous round's\n656\t    // `s_{round-1}(r)` claim. The degree is constraint_degree + 1, where + 1 is from eq term\n657\t    let mle_rounds_span =\n658\t        info_span!(\"prover.rap_constraints.mle_rounds\", phase = \"prover\").entered();\n659\t    debug!(%s_deg);\n660\t    for round in 1..=n_max {\n661\t        let sp_round_evals = prover.sumcheck_polys_batch_eval(round, r[round - 1])?;\n662\t        let batch_s = prover.compute_batch_s_poly(sp_round_evals, num_traces, round, &mu_pows);\n663\t        let batch_s_evals = (1..=s_deg)\n664\t            .map(|i| batch_s.eval_at_point(EF::from_usize(i)))\n665\t            .collect_vec();\n666\t        for &eval in &batch_s_evals {\n667\t            transcript.observe_ext(eval);\n668\t        }\n669\t        sumcheck_round_polys.push(batch_s_evals);\n670\t\n671\t        let r_round = transcript.sample_ext();\n672\t        debug!(%round, %r_round);\n673\t        r.push(r_round);\n674\t        prover.prev_s_eval = batch_s.eval_at_point(r_round);\n675\t\n676\t        prover.fold_mle_evals(round, r_round)?;\n677\t    }\n678\t    assert_eq!(r.len(), n_max + 1);\n679\t\n680\t    let column_openings = prover.into_column_openings()?;\n681\t\n682\t    let need_rot_per_trace = ctx\n683\t        .per_trace\n684\t        .iter()\n685\t        .map(|(air_idx, _)| mpk.per_air[*air_idx].vk.params.need_rot)\n686\t        .collect::<Vec<_>>();\n687\t    // Observe common main openings first, and then preprocessed/cached\n688\t    for (need_rot, openings) in need_rot_per_trace.iter().zip(column_openings.iter()) {\n689\t        for (claim, claim_rot) in column_openings_by_rot(&openings[0], *need_rot) {"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01FEaHnKTkJi1aZs7VhUfxJN","session_id":"8773bab9-c899-4b31-8324-e4269b1a66cf","uuid":"fa0a2b3a-fbd8-48e7-ba6f-c323a2551ff4","timestamp":"2026-04-15T23:13:43.367Z"}
