{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01E2avnJJA6yMrWYbpdJ9zo8","type":"tool_result","content":"55\tlet d_main_ptrs_pool: Vec<DeviceBuffer<MainMatrixPtrs<EF>>> = self.trace_metas\n56\t    .iter()\n57\t    .map(|meta| {\n58\t        let first_main_idx = usize::from(meta.has_preprocessed);\n59\t        let num_main_mats = self.mat_evals_per_trace[meta.trace_idx].len() - first_main_idx;\n60\t        DeviceBuffer::with_capacity(num_main_mats)\n61\t    })\n62\t    .collect();\n63\t```\n64\t\n65\t**Why**: Each DeviceBuffer is allocated once (total ~312 allocations for APC 300). Across 14 MLE rounds, this replaces ~4,200 allocation+free pairs per segment with ~312 one-time allocations + ~4,200 copy-only operations. Net savings: ~4,200 × 1.0μs (alloc overhead) + ~4,200 × 0.2μs (free overhead) ≈ 5ms per segment, ~10ms per proof.\n66\t\n67\t### Change 2: Replace to_device() with copy_to() in TraceCtx construction\n68\t\n69\t**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/mod.rs`, lines ~1812-1824\n70\t\n71\t**What**: Instead of `let main_ptrs_dev = main_ptrs.to_device()?;`, use `main_ptrs.copy_to(&mut d_main_ptrs_pool[meta.trace_idx])?;` and then reference `&d_main_ptrs_pool[meta.trace_idx]` in the TraceCtx.\n72\t\n73\t**Before**:\n74\t```rust\n75\tlet main_ptrs_dev = main_ptrs.to_device()?;  // allocate + copy\n76\tearly_eval.push(TraceCtx {\n77\t    // ...\n78\t    main_ptrs_dev,\n79\t    // ...\n80\t});\n81\t```\n82\t\n83\t**After**:\n84\t```rust\n85\tmain_ptrs.copy_to(&mut d_main_ptrs_pool[meta.trace_idx])?;  // copy only\n86\tearly_eval.push(TraceCtx {\n87\t    // ...\n88\t    main_ptrs_dev: unsafe {\n89\t        DeviceBuffer::non_owning(\n90\t            d_main_ptrs_pool[meta.trace_idx].as_mut_ptr(),\n91\t            main_ptrs.len(),\n92\t        )\n93\t    },\n94\t    // ..."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01FEaHnKTkJi1aZs7VhUfxJN","session_id":"8773bab9-c899-4b31-8324-e4269b1a66cf","uuid":"81e71f54-aa6d-4cef-a002-da682f144a87","timestamp":"2026-04-15T23:15:11.559Z"}
