{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01UXhBev1X1JhnqYQDuhowoV","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01N5XYspo4DV3sWX6KDT9S2f","name":"Edit","input":{"replace_all":false,"file_path":"/home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt-results/2026-04-16-0030-hoist-mle-trace-ctx-construction/plan.md","old_string":"## Rollback Criteria\n\nRevert if:\n- MLE Rounds at APC 300 improves by less than 10ms\n- STARK excl trace at APC 300 improves by less than 10ms\n- Any APC 0 regression exceeds 20ms on STARK excl trace\n- Proof verification fails at any APC configuration\n\nNote: The previous \"batch-mle-main-ptrs-upload\" (2026-04-13-1430) saved 5ms by batching uploads per round. This plan targets the ALLOCATION component that the batch approach didn't address (it still allocated fresh buffers per batch). If measured improvement is below 10ms, it confirms that cudaMallocAsync pool overhead is genuinely ~0.5μs per call (as reported), and the MLE overhead is dominated by other sources.","new_string":"## Rollback Criteria\n\nRevert if:\n- MLE Rounds at APC 300 improves by less than 3ms\n- STARK excl trace at APC 300 shows no measurable improvement (within noise)\n- Any APC 0 regression exceeds 20ms on STARK excl trace\n- Proof verification fails at any APC configuration\n\nNote: The previous \"batch-mle-main-ptrs-upload\" (2026-04-13-1430) measured total per-trace upload overhead at 5ms (0.9μs per call). This plan targets a subset of that overhead (alloc+free cycles, not the copy itself). The expected savings of 3-5ms are conservative. If improvement is below 3ms, the allocation pool is even faster than measured and further MLE overhead reduction requires targeting kernel execution time."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":375,"cache_read_input_tokens":248357,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemera