{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01QX9te4yZwWq5LtEGmZVEYt","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Report: 2026-04-13-1430-batch-mle-main-ptrs-upload\n2\t\n3\t## Description\n4\t\n5\tReplace per-trace `main_ptrs.to_device()` calls in MLE sumcheck rounds with a single batched device upload per round. Each MLE round iterates over ~310 traces (at APC 300) and calls `main_ptrs.to_device()` individually, issuing a separate `cudaMallocAsync` + `cudaMemcpyAsync` for a tiny buffer (~16-48 bytes) per trace. The plan estimated ~3000-4000 unnecessary allocation+copy+free triplets across all rounds and segments, each also acquiring the global `MEMORY_MANAGER` mutex. Consolidating all per-round main_ptrs into a single flat vector and uploading once was expected to save 20-40ms from the ~170ms MLE Rounds span at APC 300.\n6\t\n7\t## Implementation\n8\t\n9\t### Files changed\n10\t\n11\t- **`crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/batch_mle.rs`**: Changed `TraceCtx.main_ptrs_dev: DeviceBuffer<MainMatrixPtrs<EF>>` to `main_ptrs_ptr: *const MainMatrixPtrs<EF>`. Updated all consumers (`ZerocheckMleBatchBuilder::new`, `LogupMleBatchBuilder::new`, `evaluate_zerocheck_batched`, `evaluate_single_logup`) to use `t.main_ptrs_ptr` instead of `t.main_ptrs_dev.as_ptr()`.\n12\t\n13\t- **`crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/batch_mle_monomial.rs`**: Updated `ZerocheckMonomialBatch::new`, `ZerocheckMonomialParYBatch::new`, `LogupMonomialBatch::new` to use `t.main_ptrs_ptr` instead of `t.main_ptrs_dev.as_ptr()`. Updated doc comment referencing `main_ptrs_dev`.\n14\t\n15\t- **`crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/mle_round.rs`**: Changed `evaluate_mle_constraints_gpu` and `evaluate_mle_interactions_gpu` parameter from `&DeviceBuffer<MainMatrixPtrs<EF>>` to `*const MainMatrixPtrs<EF>`, removing the `.as_ptr()` indirection inside.\n16\t\n17\t- **`crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/mod.rs`**: In `sumcheck_polys_batch_eval()`:\n18\t  - **Case A (late_eval)**: Collect all main_ptrs into `all_late_main_ptrs: Vec<MainMatrixPtrs<EF>>` with per-trace offsets during the loop. After the loop, do a single `to_device()` and backfill pointers into each `TraceCtx.main_ptrs_ptr`. Keep the `DeviceBuffer` alive via `_keepalive_late_main_ptrs`.\n19\t  - **Case B (early_eval)**: Same pattern — collect into `all_early_main_ptrs` with offsets, single `to_device()` after Phase 3 loop, backfill pointers, keep alive via `_keepalive_early_main_ptrs`.\n20\t\n21\t- **`crates/cuda-backend/src/tests.rs`**: Updated `test_monomial_vs_dag_equivalence` to use `main_ptrs_ptr: _main_ptrs_dev.as_ptr()` and keep the `DeviceBuffer` alive via `_main_ptrs_dev`.\n22\t\n23\t### Key decisions\n24\t\n25\t- Used the backfill approach: push TraceCtx with `main_ptrs_ptr: null()`, then overwrite after the batch upload. This avoids restructuring the existing loop logic.\n26\t- No deviations from the plan.\n27\t\n28\t## Results\n29\t\n30\t### APC 300\n31\t\n32\t| Metric | Baseline | Before Task | After Task | vs Baseline | vs Before |\n33\t|--------|----------|-------------|------------|-------------|-----------|\n34\t| STARK excl trace | 2455ms | 1417ms | 1421ms | -1034ms, 1.73x lower | +4ms, 1.00x (noise) |\n35\t| MLE Rounds | 180ms | 170ms | 165ms | -15ms, 1.09x lower | -5ms, 1.03x lower |\n36\t| Round 0 | 662ms | 295ms | 296ms | -366ms, 2.24x lower | +1ms, 1.00x (noise) |\n37\t| LogUp GKR | 790ms | 518ms | 533ms | -257ms, 1.48x lower | +15ms (noise) |\n38\t\n39\t### APC 100\n40\t\n41\t| Metric | Baseline | Before Task | After Task | vs Baseline | vs Before |\n42\t|--------|----------|-------------|------------|-------------|-----------|\n43\t| STARK excl trace | 2155ms | 1583ms | 1593ms | -562ms, 1.35x lower | +10ms, 1.01x (noise) |\n44\t| MLE Rounds | 150ms | 140ms | 135ms | -15ms, 1.11x lower | -5ms, 1.04x lower |\n45\t\n46\t### APC 0\n47\t\n48\t| Metric | Baseline | Before Task | After Task | vs Baseline | vs Before |\n49\t|--------|----------|-------------|------------|-------------|-----------|\n50\t| STARK excl trace | 2153ms | 2147ms | 2150ms | -3ms, 1.00x | +3ms, 1.00x (noise) |\n51\t| MLE Rounds | 118ms | 114ms | 113ms | -5ms, 1.04x lower | -1ms, 1.01x lower |\n52\t\n53\t### CUDA API call counts (from nsys)\n54\t\n55\t| Metric | Before | After | Delta |\n56\t|--------|--------|-------|-------|\n57\t| H2D copies | 30,035 | 24,436 | -5,599 |\n58\t\n59\t## Assessment\n60\t\n61\t**The optimization did NOT meet its success criteria.** MLE Rounds at APC 300 improved by only 5ms (170ms → 165ms), well below the plan's 10ms rollback threshold. STARK excl trace showed no net improvement (+4ms, within noise).\n62\t\n63\tThe nsys data confirms the batching is mechanically correct: ~5,600 fewer H2D copy calls. However, the per-call overhead of these small uploads was much lower than estimated:\n64\t- **Estimated**: ~15-20μs per call (mutex + cudaMallocAsync + cudaMemcpyAsync + cudaFreeAsync + HashMap ops)\n65\t- **Actual**: ~1μs per call (5ms improvement / 5600 eliminated calls ≈ 0.9μs each)\n66\t\n67\tThe discrepancy is likely because:\n68\t1. `cudaMallocAsync` with small allocations may be served from a pool cache, avoiding actual allocation\n69\t2. The MEMORY_MANAGER mutex is uncontended in the single-threaded MLE rounds path (unlike multi-stream Round 0/GKR)\n70\t3. `cudaMemcpyAsync` for 16-48 bytes is essentially free on the PCIe bus\n71\t\n72\tNo regression at APC 0 (MLE Rounds -1ms, STARK excl trace +3ms, both noise).\n73\t\n74\tPer rollback criterion #1 (MLE Rounds improvement < 10ms), this optimization is **reverted**.\n75\t\n76\t## Future Work\n77\t\n78\t- **What worked**: The batching pattern is sound and the code change is minimal/clean. The `_keepalive` pattern for shared device buffers with raw pointer offsets is reusable.\n79\t- **Root cause of small impact**: The MLE rounds path is single-threaded, so mutex contention is near-zero. The dominant MLE Rounds cost is GPU kernel execution, not CUDA API overhead.\n80\t- **More impactful MLE Rounds targets**: The remaining 165ms is dominated by actual kernel execution time across ~16 invocations of `sumcheck_polys_batch_eval`. Further improvement would require:\n81\t  - Reducing the number of MLE rounds (algorithmic change)\n82\t  - Making the per-round GPU kernels faster (kernel optimization)\n83\t  - Batching the evaluation kernels themselves across traces (not just the upload)\n84\t- **Potential combination**: This optimization could be combined with multi-stream MLE rounds if that approach is pursued, where mutex contention would be higher and the per-call overhead would increase.\n85\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01XTGZhu6iHsGAEo43rpScFd","session_id":"8773bab9-c899-4b31-8324-e4269b1a66cf","uuid":"71660947-00d8-4755-8c44-684253f7023a","timestamp":"2026-04-15T23:19:35.729Z"}
